## Remediation

18 clips re-baked with `scripts/generate-pack-audio.py --tts qwen3 --language japanese
--speaker ono_anna --force --jobs 1 --worker-python ~/.venvs/qwen-tts/bin/python
--only <19 ids>` (controller-launched wave 17:38-17:57, 18/19 green; `ja.lex.home.fukimasu`
FAILED: "6.5 s still exceeds 3.0 s cap after retries (runaway output)").
Retry #2 (this lane, qwen3, ~30 min under load 25-30): first take runaway again, resample
request died with "worker noise" → FAILED, wav removed.
Retry #3 switched engine per lts-pack-audio-qa rule ("switch to a genuinely different
engine rather than more attempts"): `--tts kokoro` (sherpa-onnx kokoro-multi-lang-v1_1,
the repo's pinned pre-switch payload) → generated, row written by the generator,
sha256/bytes verified equal to disk. Owner rule 2026-11-17 permits any voice for
word/drill clips, so the ono_anna→kokoro engine switch on this single drill word is
policy-legal. Provenance in the row names the actual runtime.

Race note (honesty): an intermediate kokoro pass collided with the still-draining qwen3
retry's final manifest write (last-writer kept the old fukimasu row); re-running the
deterministic kokoro bake rewrote the row correctly. Final manifest state is verified
row-by-row: all 19 rewritten rows match disk sha256/bytes, all other 4916 rows are
byte-identical to HEAD (git diff: 18 insertions/18 deletions after the kokoro wave,
19/19 after the fukimasu row landed). No backup was needed from
~/.hermes/cache/scratch/k65/backup/ (holds the pre-fix wavs + manifest).

